-- The R4 verdict seam: a scope-IMPLIES-requirement rule.
--
-- If the tenancy is a residential tenancy, the landlord must have given
-- written notice of at least two months. The docassemble backend must NOT
-- lower the top-level IMPLIES to the classical `not scope or requirement`
-- driver: it must emit scope and requirement as separate seekable
-- variables, ask the scope question first, and report a verdict, so that
-- "the rule never reached you" (NotApplicable) is distinguishable from
-- "you complied" (Complies) — both of which are TRUE to the classical
-- #EVALs below.

DECLARE Tenancy
    HAS
      @desc Whether the letting is of a dwelling occupied as a home
      `is a residential tenancy` IS A BOOLEAN
      @desc Whether the landlord served notice to quit in writing
      `written notice was given` IS A BOOLEAN
      @desc Length of the notice period served, in whole months
      `months of notice given`   IS A NUMBER

@export Whether the landlord notice rule is satisfied for this tenancy
GIVEN t IS A Tenancy @desc The tenancy under assessment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `notice rule satisfied` t IF
    `the rule applies` IMPLIES `the notice requirement is met`
 WHERE
    `the rule applies` MEANS
        t's `is a residential tenancy`

    `the notice requirement is met` MEANS
            t's `written notice was given`
        AND t's `months of notice given` AT LEAST 2

-- Complies: residential, written notice, three months.
#EVAL `notice rule satisfied` OF
        Tenancy
        WITH
            `is a residential tenancy` IS TRUE
            `written notice was given` IS TRUE
            `months of notice given`   IS 3
-- TRUE  (docassemble verdict: Complies)

-- InBreach: residential, written notice, but only one month.
#EVAL `notice rule satisfied` OF
        Tenancy
        WITH
            `is a residential tenancy` IS TRUE
            `written notice was given` IS TRUE
            `months of notice given`   IS 1
-- FALSE  (docassemble verdict: InBreach)

-- NotApplicable: not a residential tenancy; classically vacuous TRUE.
-- In the emitted interview NO requirement question may be asked on this
-- path — the roundtrip fixture for this case deliberately carries only
-- the scope answer, so any requirement question fails the harness.
#EVAL `notice rule satisfied` OF
        Tenancy
        WITH
            `is a residential tenancy` IS FALSE
            `written notice was given` IS FALSE
            `months of notice given`   IS 0
-- TRUE  (docassemble verdict: NotApplicable)
